        <h2>2. What the Service is</h2>
        <p>
          AdaptiveResume is a resume completeness tool. You upload up to three resumes and, if you
          like, your LinkedIn resume export, which is the PDF containing your work experience. Either
          kind of file alone is enough to start. We identify skills, credentials, and standards you
          may have left off, and you confirm, edit, or skip every single item. Nothing appears on
          your resume without your confirmation. Your finished resume is delivered as a downloadable
          DOCX and PDF. The $149 targeted build additionally analyzes one job posting you provide,
          lists which of its requirements your confirmed items cover and which have no matching
          confirmed item, and prepares 25 role-specific interview questions, each showing the
          posting requirement and the confirmed resume lines it comes from. It does not provide
          answers, answer guidance, or coaching. Before you purchase a build, you can try two things
          at no cost.
          The free scan runs a set of formatting and structure checks on your resume and does not
          suggest any content. The demo walks you through a sample review using a fictional profile;
          it does not use any of your information and never contacts our server.
        </p>

        <h2>3. What the Service is not</h2>
        <p>
